  "method": [
    "For each requested height, mapped its x position into the registered source panel and inspected dark-pixel row locations together with the source raster.",
    "Tracked each of the three solid and three dashed traces from its axis intercept, using neighboring x columns to resolve gaps in dashed lines and crossings. Local interpolation across a printed dash gap is raster trace reconstruction, not interpolation of a previous target table.",
    "Excluded vertical/horizontal dotted grid pixels and panel border pixels. Values are rounded to 0.005/0.01; the raster does not support manufacturing-level or exact 0.1 percentage-point accuracy.",
    "No published curve is extrapolated beyond its endpoint. f/5.6 stops near h=.68 and f/8 near h=.78. f/22 is published to h=1.0.",
    "This denser audit supersedes target_manual_audited.json when they differ. In particular f/22 h=.4 20T is approximately .455, and f/8 h=.78 10T approximately .205; first sparse audit was less certain about these dashed traces.",
    "Source focusing rule: maximum on-axis 20 lp/mm MTF at f/5.6; one image plane retained for the other apertures. Final comparison must also audit actual ray-traced image heights, rather than assuming h maps exactly through atan(193*h/148.1).",
    "Dense sampled superiority is stronger evidence than the earlier seven-height comparison, but does not mathematically certify the continuous curves between samples or eliminate scan-reading uncertainty."
